 straight past Fernwick and never know it's here."]},{"id":"tamsin","role":"Picker","wander":[1104.0,272.0,1360.0,556.8],"says":["Mind the windfalls, they're slippery. And full of wasps.","One for the basket, one for me. Bram never counts."]},{"id":"kit","role":"Apple boy","wander":[176.0,851.2,1296.0,915.2],"says":["Orchard to the stall, stall to the orchard. My legs'll be worn to stumps by harvest.","Riverhold's only through the wood, if you know the way. I've been twice!"]},{"id":"osric","role":"Woodcutter","post":[224.0,505.6],"facing":"down","says":["The ferns grow so thick in the deep wood you can lose a dog in them. I have.","Every stick of firewood in Fernwick came off my axe. Winter's coming, mark me."]},{"id":"dora","role":"Gardener","wander":[176.0,1008.0,368.0,1200.0],"chore":"water","says":"Carrots and beets, every morning, before the sun gets on them. Kit! Stop eating the stock!"},{"id":"gideon","role":"Field hand","wander":[176.0,1328.0,368.0,1520.0],"chore":"hoe","says":["The melons are coming on. Don't tell anyone, they'll all want one.","Weeds grow in this soil like nothing else. So does everything, mind."]},{"id":"pip","role":"Field hand","wander":[560.0,1392.0,688.0,1552.0],"chore":"dig","says":"Corn's up past my shoulder. Another fortnight and we'll lose the scarecrow in it."},{"id":"mabel","role":"Woodcutter's sister","wander":[560.0,1072.0,688.0,1264.0],"chore":"water","says":"The potatoes are only just showing. Walk in the furrows, please, not on them."},{"id":"ezra","role":"Farmer","wander":[1456.0,496.0,1648.0,688.0],"chore":"hoe","says":["The wheat's mine and the grain's my brother's. He'll say it's the other way round.","Wolves came down to the barn in the spring. Haven't been back since we built the fence higher."]},{"id":"cole","role":"Farmer","wander":[1840.0,496.0,2000.0,688.0],"chore":"dig","says":"Ezra's wheat, is it? Ha. Who sowed it? Who's digging his turnips for him right now?"},{"id":"hester","role":"Village elder","post":[819.2,979.2],"facing":"down","chore":"sit","says":["I've fed the ducks on this pond since I was a girl. Never seen a duck. I live in hope.","Fernwick's named for the ferns, dear. They grow so tall round here, the wood hides us. We like it that way."]},{"id":"abel","role":"Cowman","post":[1427.2,1382.4],"facing":"down","chore":"sit","says":"Milking's done, mucking out's done. Now I sit. That's the order of things."},{"id":"ruth","role":"Villager","wander":[784.0,940.8,1296.0,985.6],"says":["The well water's cold as winter even in high summer. Have a drink.","My two boys argue over that wheat every evening. Their father left it to both of them."]},{"id":"wat","role":"Barn hand","post":[1548.8,1241.6],"facing":"down","says":"Four cows, two pigs and a goat that hates me. Barn's not big, but it's full."},{"id":"nan","role":"Bram's mother","wander":[1104.0,656.0,1264.0,752.0],"chore":"water","says":"Peppers in front, carrots behind, and the beets wherever they like. A garden's a stubborn thing."},{"id":"jem","role":"Field hand","wander":[1520.0,1520.0,2000.0,1584.0],"chore":"hoe","says":["Potatoes are up and in the barn. Now I turn it over for the winter wheat.","Hal Furrow over in Seacombe's my cousin. Long way west, that. I've never been."]}],"facing":"right","lights":[[272,744,"window"],[400,744,"window"],[560,723,"window"],[704,744,"window"],[800,744,"window"],[966,744,"window"]]}